.TH LIBEMAIL\-CLIENT 3 "" "email-cli" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
libemail\-client \- send and read mail through IMAP, SMTP or the Gmail API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <email-client.h>
.sp
.B emc_status emc_open(emc_client **out, const emc_account *account);
.B emc_status emc_send(emc_client *c, const emc_message *m, emc_send_result *r);
.B emc_status emc_list_folders(emc_client *c, char ***names, int *count);
.B emc_status emc_list_messages(emc_client *c, const char *folder,
.B                              int unseen_only, char ***ids, int *count);
.B emc_status emc_fetch_message(emc_client *c, const char *folder,
.B                              const char *id, char **raw);
.B void emc_close(emc_client *c);
.sp
cc ... $(pkg-config --cflags --libs libemail-client)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libemail\-client
holds the mail client logic of
.BR email\-cli (1)
once, so that other programs send and read mail natively.
.PP
.B emc_open
copies an account (IMAP/SMTP, or Gmail with an OAuth2 refresh token) and
opens no connection; the network is used when an operation needs it.
.B emc_send
sends a message and returns the outcome and the Message-ID in an
.IR emc_send_result .
IMAP accounts send through SMTP over TLS, Gmail accounts through the Gmail
REST API.
.B emc_list_folders ,
.B emc_list_messages
and
.B emc_fetch_message
read.  Arrays returned are released with
.BR emc_free_list ;
a fetched message with
.BR free (3).
.PP
The library does not audit: the calling program records what it sent, to
whom and when, from the returned outcome and message id.  It reads no
configuration file, never prompts, and verifies the server certificate unless
.I insecure_tls
is set (test servers only).  A handle is not thread safe.
.PP
A verified server certificate is also checked for revocation: OCSP first, at
the responder the certificate names, then the CRL it names (cached with its
validity; an expired CRL counts as none).  A certificate known to be revoked
is refused.  When neither source can be used the connection goes on, with an
error\-level log entry and a notice that
.B emc_take_security_notice
returns (1 and the text, then cleared; 0 when none), at most once per
certificate and 6 hours.  The CRL cache and the record of signals live under
\fI/email\-cli/revocation\fR.  \fISSL_CERT_FILE\fR, when set,
names the trusted certificates of every connection.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Every operation returns an
.I emc_status
(\fBEMC_OK\fR on success); \fBemc_strerror\fR describes it and
\fBemc_last_error\fR gives the detail of the last failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli (1)
